codex
The ARM `X(bfi)` mask reaches all three requested UB forms. The M88K rotate mask reaches signed overflow at count 31, but its zero-count guard prevents a shift by 32. I also found device masks whose counts come directly from register data.

Several apparent hazards are guarded: SHAD/SHLD handle zero separately, MIPS page-mask decoding rejects unsupported masks before deriving later counts, and both integer-to-double helpers handle `INT64_MIN` before counting significant bits.

