The MIPS enumeration needs a qualification: ordinary DEXT has no bad count. DEXTM and DEXTU each have 496 invalid field combinations out of 1,024, and the cast converts their negative counts into oversized unsigned counts. ARM BFI also fails at the valid full-width case, which gives it stronger correctness priority than an invalid MIPS encoding.

