**The eight unresolved operators**

Their arithmetic is not mysterious; their complete caller reachability is unfinished.

| Operators | Existence boundary | What prevents a confident reachability verdict |
|---|---|---|
| NE2000’s three `8*i` shifts | **b** when `i >= 8`; device-window dispatch can accommodate more than eight bytes | Ordinary scalar accesses are bounded. Larger debugger/loader/Jazz DMA accesses commonly carry `NO_EXCEPTIONS`, and this device lacks `DM_READS_HAVE_NO_SIDE_EFFECTS`, so those apparent routes do **not** establish execution |
| i80321’s `idata >> (i*8)` | **b** when `i >= 8` | No local eight-byte limit; ordinary contained ARM register accesses do not establish that iteration |
| SH4’s four BSC lane shifts | In BE mode, **b** when `len >= 10` | Partial-access rejection establishes a lower bound only. Scalar accesses are bounded; a larger transfer reaching these exact register cases still needs a proven route |

I would not file these as **confirmed guest-reachable defects**, and I would not mark them `NONE`. Their unresolved status is why this report does not claim closure.

