**What I would not file**

I would not file the 313 regression-source occurrences as additional emulator defects. The 29 support-file occurrences are in `diff_footbridge.c`, `diff_ieee_store.c`, `diff_m8820x.c`, `diff_m8invread.c`, `diff_memory_rw.c`, `diff_wdc_identify.c`, `repro_m8invread.c`, and `repro_m8sarpurge.c`. The other 284 are retained artifact/check sources, including deliberately preserved baselines and variants. They remain in the textual denominator; I have not presented them as a complete separate correctness audit of the regression programs.

I would also exclude these tempting false positives from the issue queue:

| Site | Why it does not support the proposed filing |
|---|---|
| `net.c` broadcast mask | Effective upper clamp is **8** |
| Ordinary DEXT | Its actual decoder produces counts **1…63** |
| INS middle shifts | Enumeration gives **31−msb**, always **0…31**, even for reversed fields |
| ARM Thumb `imm6` | Despite its name, the decode is five bits; zero has separate semantics |
| ARM load/store rotations | Both paths guard `rot_sh != 0` |
| M88K `imm16 << shift` | `imm16` is **uint32_t**, despite containing a sign-extended value |
| MIPS branch-immediate alignment shifts | The decoder’s `imm` is **uint32_t** |
| MIPS TLB probe’s `found << R2K3K_INDEX_SHIFT` | `found == -1` takes the other branch before the shift |
| MIPS page-size masks | The page-mask switch rejects unsupported values before later shifts |
| Alpha high-part INS/EXT/MSK | Explicit zero/64 handling excludes count 64 |
| PPC `ppc_single_narrow` | Excessive shifts return before mask construction |
| PPC `rldimi` count | Enumerating the post-decrement loop state still keeps the later mask count **0…63** |
| PCC2 warning masks | Fixed enum callers; byte-offset mask has a preceding modulo-64 operation |
| SYSASIC event mask | Actual call arguments avoid bit 31; the macro’s nominal range alone would overstate reachability |
| ARC cache-key macros | No production expansion; nominal large count fields are not an executed defect |
| PMAG-JA pixel shift | Compiled out by `#if 0` |
| Eight unresolved wider-access shifts | Neither a proven guest route nor a sufficient global bound has been established |

**The 16-bit-`unsigned int` qualification**

`1U` is not a universal replacement. The already-unsigned ARM UBFX/SBFX masks, M88K `1U << d`, generated ARM carry masks, GD-ROM/SH4 warning masks, and LCA’s `0x800U << dev` can exceed a 16-bit unsigned operand’s width.

There are also numerous plain-`int` assumptions, including `1 << DYNTRANS_L1N` with count 17. Consequently, the `NONE` totals above are explicitly **not an arbitrary-C99-host portability certificate**. For repairs intended to support the architectural 32-bit mask independently of `unsigned int` width, use the architectural-width operand before shifting, together with any necessary count or field validation.

Finally, one definite additional finding deserves its own correctness row: [PPC `X(rldicl)`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c) initializes `tmp2 = 0`, ORs the mask into **`tmp`**, and assigns `tmp & tmp2` to the destination. It therefore **always writes zero**. The computed count is safe; the mask is accumulated into the wrong variable. This is **CRITICAL and EASY**, independently of the shift-UB census.
